    t104: "Do I have to scan everything myself?", t105: "No. You add papers as they come: a photo when a letter arrives, a forwarded email for an invoice. Lucien also recognises your contracts from bank debits and offers to add the missing paper.",
    t106: "What if the AI gets a date wrong?", t107: "Every extracted field is shown with its confidence level. You correct it with one tap and the reminders recalculate. No deadline is created on a date you couldn't see.",
    t108: "Does Lucien have access to my bank account?", t109: "You choose: import a statement (CSV or PDF) or connect your bank through a licensed aggregator (Enable Banking). In that case Lucien only receives the list of transactions, read-only. It can neither pay nor transfer, and never knows your credentials.",
    t110: "How does Lucien count savings?", t111: "Every action (cancel, renegotiate, remove a duplicate) carries a yearly gain estimated from your own debits. The counter on the home screen only adds up the actions you have confirmed as done. It never inflates with assumptions.",
    t112: "How is it different from a budgeting app?", t113: "A budgeting app tells you how much you spent. Lucien tells you what to cancel, before which date, how much you gain, and writes the letter. It links spending to contracts, which a budgeting app cannot do.",
    t114: "How does the AI connector work?", t115: "You add Lucien as a connector in your assistant (Claude, ChatGPT, and any MCP-compatible tool). The assistant can then consult your papers and deadlines to answer you. It cannot change anything, nor reach the folders you excluded. Every consultation appears in your log.",
    t116: "Can I manage my parents' paperwork?", t117: "Yes, with a paid plan: a space per person you help, rights per folder, and reminders that reach the carer. Two conditions, because the law protects the people being helped: the person must give consent in Lucien (and can withdraw it at any time), and their bank can only be connected by themselves or their legal representative. If they are under guardianship, the guardian authorises access, within the limits of their mandate.",
